<title>USA: Senate commerce panel sets vote on Garvey for FAA.</title>
<headline>Senate commerce panel sets vote on Garvey for FAA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Senate Commerce Committee said Monday it had scheduled a vote for Wednesday on the nomination of Jane Garvey to head the Federal Aviation Administration.</p>
<p>Garvey, a former director of Boston's Logan Airport, got a sympathetic hearing when she appeared before the panel in June. Her nomination is expected to go to the full Senate with the committee's backing.</p>
<p>The job of FAA administrator became vacant last November with the departure of David Hinson after three years in the position. Barry Valentine has been acting in the post since then.</p>
</text>
